-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----

Placeholder — replace with the real SnappyMail release-signing public
key before building. The build stage refuses to run against this file
(it is smaller than 100 bytes and cannot be imported by gpg).

Steps to install the correct key:

  1. Fetch the key from the SnappyMail project website
     (https://snappymail.eu/) or the maintainer's published channel.

  2. Verify the fingerprint against the fingerprint published on the
     project website / in the release notes. Cross-check with a second
     independent source if possible (a mirror, the maintainer's other
     public accounts).

  3. Once the fingerprint matches, overwrite this file with the ASCII-
     armoured public key block (the `-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY
     BLOCK-----` … `-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----` section).

  4. Commit the change to git — key rotations are deliberate,
     audit-visible operations, not silent keyserver-fetches.

Any downgrade of this file back to a placeholder must be treated as a
security incident: it disables SnappyMail release-signature verification
across every future build.
-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
